{"steamid": "76561198014909616", "personaname": "Ivan Kersovic", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/IvanKersovic/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 3, "playtime_forever": 5174, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5174, "last_played": 1673127695, "avatar": "108de593486643ed0e7fdd7830ef42aa5d3e3026"}, "language": "english", "review": "This is a mixed bag of a game, but overall I think it just about edges it into a favourable review, given the price it is sold at on sale. \n\nObviously it is an unfinished game that will never be finished -the first in a planned trilogy that will never be completed, with unplanned DLC. But it does have an ending that is meaningful even if it is short.\n\nIt goes crazy on side quests and although the game guilts you into doing them for fear of dire consequences, most of the side quests have no meaningful impact on the story. \n\nThe actual mechanics of the fighting, the abilities, the worlds are pretty cool. Some changes from the original trilogy were improvements, some were worse, but that's true of every ME game. Some of the characters were likeable, some were really bad.\n\nAnimations were fixed somewhat from launch but there's still a few horrible moments where your character is supposed to be looking kindly at someone and it looks like you're going to go at them with your teeth.\n\nI put 86 hours into this game - I think it would be a better game at 30 hours long rather than nearly 90. Most of the additional content was repetitive or uninteresting but it's hard to tell what you should devote time to. I mostly put the extra hours in because I enjoy the lore.", "timestamp_created": 1673129170, "timestamp_updated": 1673129170, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.522648870944976807", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "130380570", "author": {"steamid": "76561199091844039", "personaname": "Beltzebrute", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199091844039/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 11522, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1766, "last_played": 1703334470, "avatar": "d1d63486ff8e79413805d307441e001e76d69585"}, "language": "english", "review": "Bugs are gone, characters don't look as awful as the initial release, game is loads of fun and engaging. Might not be as good as the Trilogy, but I still feel this is a strong entry into the series. Separate from it but in a way that still makes it feel relevant.", "timestamp_created": 1673126397, "timestamp_updated": 1673126397, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "130375467", "author": {"steamid": "76561198024000113", "personaname": "NiteKnight", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198024000113/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 19, "playtime_forever": 3076, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 724, "last_played": 1728178830, "avatar": "fbc5e0c51f5b2e9cca653592d1be35170c4c4605"}, "language": "english", "review": " Andromeda does not come anywhere close to the others Mass Effect games and is a great disappointment.  The game is totally unworthy of the name Mass Effect, shame on you Bio Ware.", "timestamp_created": 1673121605, "timestamp_updated": 1673121605, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.525846719741821289", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "r